{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-11","kind":"proposition","title":"比例关系保持可公度与不可公度","englishTitle":"If four magnitudes be proportional, and the first be commensurable with the second, the third will also be commensurable with the fourth; and, if the first be incommensurable with the second, the third will also be incommensurable with the fourth.","book":10,"number":11,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":11,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","contentId":"euclid-10-11","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a01016596179cb001ded17221c910e471ec953ae9e185bb488ca671ad7b27f94","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-11.statement","euclid-10-11.construction.1","euclid-10-11.proof.1","euclid-10-11.proof.2","euclid-10-11.proof.3","euclid-10-11.proof.4","euclid-10-11.proof.5","euclid-10-11.conclusion","euclid-10-11.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-11.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3d54ce8d144c8098ae5ba814952de708d82d20efb3a898247cb8b917b948d372","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If four magnitudes be proportional, and the first be commensurable with the second, the third will also be commensurable with the fourth; and, if the first be incommensurable with the second, the third will also be incommensurable with the fourth."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果四级为成比例, 第一类为可公度, 第二类为可公度, 第三项为可公度;如果第一项为不可公度, 第二类为不可公度, 第三项为不可公度, 第四个为不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"adc8e10e00208427e12f5fce9188314d22f9c71fdaa4c168c85534151b91928f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let A, B, C, D be four magnitudes in proportion, so that, as A is to B, so is C to D, and let A be commensurable with B; I say that C will also be commensurable with D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让A,B,C,D成四级,A比B等于C比D,A比A比B;我说C比A比D；A 与 B 之比等于 C 与 D 之比；上述对应量可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e12af796e0f6e13130c8a98a9db52788ad901e26bd0f3053200af4bfe47a9d0f","citations":["euclid-10-5"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since A is commensurable with B, therefore A has to B the ratio which a number has to a number. [[X. 5](/principles/euclid-10-5)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为A是可公度,B,A的比例为B,一个数字等于一个数字。 [[X. 5](/principles/euclid-10-5)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"24866b5ef56eb127a3625a438999a7a000214ee4a5db9091ef18f54a4757a3f7","citations":["euclid-10-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, as A is to B, so is C to D; therefore C also has to D the ratio which a number has to a number; therefore C is commensurable with D. [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A比B等于C比D,因此C比D,一个数字等于D,C比C,C比D；A 与 B 之比等于 C 与 D 之比；上述对应量可公度。 [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6b92a5cb462d8720209b20b6494e42df360fb1c6e9b036a7d26155baccdc4eeb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Next, let A be incommensurable with B; I say that C will also be incommensurable with D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来,A比不可公度比B;我说C也比A比D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a7679752f039632af37d342d3071bdf5ed8dc513bf4ad1f4ffe5ca96f590d535","citations":["euclid-10-7"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since A is incommensurable with B, therefore A has not to B the ratio which a number has to a number. [[X. 7](/principles/euclid-10-7)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为A是不可公度,B,因此A没有达到B,这个数字是多少。 [[X. 7](/principles/euclid-10-7)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"80b221ede009668d6f8ae07f2c95c30b75c521cd7597df94e70d310f1842fbe7","citations":["euclid-10-8"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, as A is to B, so is C to D; therefore neither has C to D the ratio which a number has to a number; therefore C is incommensurable with D. [[X. 8](/principles/euclid-10-8)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A比B等于C比D,因此,数字与数字之比也为C比D,因此C比D,C比D；A 与 B 之比等于 C 与 D 之比；上述对应量不可公度。 [[X. 8](/principles/euclid-10-8)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":7,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d0def46992eb0b105b82d6bce6477450c524a884c436026a0e1ed896becf6c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-11.source","contentId":"euclid-10-11","revisionId":"euclid-10-11@raw-a01016596179cb00","order":8,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7c15a89d66f8791b1a573d3562d7a79a0869e8e414972976e6a96f51a4ddb597","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-11:euclid-10-5:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-11.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-5","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop